00:13:48.140 --> 00:13:49.430
This is...

00:13:48.180 --> 00:13:48.220
{=1}FIRE SPRINKLERS ARE
MALFUNCTIONING DUE TO HEAT.

00:13:50.850 --> 00:13:52.810
A fire on the first floor of a high-rise

00:13:52.810 --> 00:13:55.940
with a large number of people
still on the upper floors.

00:13:55.940 --> 00:14:00.570
There's no guarantee that there won't be
any casualties before the firefighters arrive.

00:14:00.570 --> 00:14:04.200
Not only that, but this is no ordinary fire.

00:14:04.200 --> 00:14:05.870
I felt a powerful spell being cast...

00:14:05.870 --> 00:14:09.290
just before the alarm went off.

00:14:09.290 --> 00:14:10.580
There's no question.

00:14:10.580 --> 00:14:14.830
This fire was triggered by a magician
with devastating power!

00:14:17.340 --> 00:14:21.130
Burn, burn! Are you watching,
Magicians' Association?

00:14:21.130 --> 00:14:26.760
You mocked me for only being able
to burn things! Well, this is my magic!

00:14:29.060 --> 00:14:30.930
How deranged he is.

00:14:30.930 --> 00:14:32.810
I feel ill.

00:14:32.810 --> 00:14:35.270
How dare he use magic to commit a crime!

00:14:36.190 --> 00:14:38.650
That's absolutely unforgivable.

00:14:38.650 --> 00:14:42.950
This is the duty I charged myself with.

00:14:42.950 --> 00:14:46.990
So that magicians can exist as humans,
rather than as weapons.

00:14:46.990 --> 00:14:52.450
That's what my brother and I are striving
to define as the role of the Magician!

00:14:52.450 --> 00:14:54.750
Inject the CAD with Psions.

00:14:54.750 --> 00:14:57.540
Activation sequence, commencing output.

00:15:00.840 --> 00:15:02.920
Confirming coordinates.

00:15:02.920 --> 00:15:05.340
Outputting magic sequence.

00:15:06.300 --> 00:15:07.850
Targeting the Eidos.

00:15:07.850 --> 00:15:09.600
Magic, activated!

00:15:09.600 --> 00:15:12.060
Now rewriting actual phenomena!

00:15:18.610 --> 00:15:21.400
Impossible! What the hell is going on?

00:15:21.400 --> 00:15:23.820
Just what I'd expect of you, Brother.

00:15:23.820 --> 00:15:26.200
Your CAD adjustments are flawless.

00:15:26.200 --> 00:15:27.410
Who are you?

00:15:27.410 --> 00:15:29.370
I'd like to ask the same of you.

00:15:29.370 --> 00:15:32.200
Using magic to commit arson...

00:15:32.200 --> 00:15:34.960
That's an unforgivable act!

00:15:34.960 --> 00:15:37.290
Shut up, you little brat!

00:15:37.290 --> 00:15:39.420
You seem to be capable of some magic,

00:15:39.420 --> 00:15:42.670
but as someone who's undergone reinforcements,
I'm an upper-level magician!

00:15:42.670 --> 00:15:45.630
You can just lament the fact
that you didn't know your place!

00:15:48.340 --> 00:15:51.390
What the hell is that look in your eyes?

00:15:51.390 --> 00:15:53.600
Mommy, where are you?

00:15:54.560 --> 00:15:56.390
Mommy!

00:15:56.390 --> 00:15:58.310
No!

00:16:20.790 --> 00:16:22.630
You're safe now.

00:16:24.130 --> 00:16:26.170
Just wait a little, all right?

00:16:26.170 --> 00:16:28.590
Let's look for your mother together.

00:16:42.110 --> 00:16:44.360
What? Don't tell me this is...

00:16:44.360 --> 00:16:46.150
Area interference?

00:16:46.150 --> 00:16:50.360
Arson via magic, an attack on a young child...

00:16:50.360 --> 00:16:54.280
And how dare you... How dare you...

00:16:54.280 --> 00:16:57.080
destroy the hair ornament
my brother gave me!

00:16:57.870 --> 00:17:00.170
S-Stay away from me!

00:17:03.040 --> 00:17:05.000
Even if magic doesn't work...

00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:07.300
this should!

00:17:07.300 --> 00:17:10.880
Did you think you could win
if they were live bullets?

00:17:10.880 --> 00:17:13.970
I've suppressed all flammable phenomena.

00:17:13.970 --> 00:17:16.310
Explosives cannot be ignited.

00:17:18.140 --> 00:17:20.890
I-Is that a genuine...

00:17:20.890 --> 00:17:23.520
upper-level magician?

00:17:23.520 --> 00:17:25.360
You fool.

00:17:25.360 --> 00:17:26.820
Stop!

00:17:29.240 --> 00:17:31.030
Miyuki!

00:17:31.030 --> 00:17:32.360
Brother!

00:17:32.360 --> 00:17:35.240
Miyuki, we're going to get out of here now.

00:17:35.240 --> 00:17:36.450
Even for an emergency...

00:17:36.450 --> 00:17:40.370
that was too much of a display to put on
this close to the Magicians' Association branch.

00:17:40.370 --> 00:17:44.380
The magic surveillance network here
is far more dense than in the city!

00:17:44.380 --> 00:17:46.840
We'll talk later! Come on!

00:17:49.840 --> 00:17:53.010
I've disabled the video
of the surveillance system.

00:17:53.010 --> 00:17:54.970
And though there were
no signs of any other people,

00:17:54.970 --> 00:17:57.680
we'll have to ask our aunt
to monitor the internet.

00:17:58.930 --> 00:18:00.480
Don't worry.

00:18:00.480 --> 00:18:03.770
There won't be any trouble with Aunt Maya.

00:18:03.770 --> 00:18:07.820
Since it was our aunt who
requested us to target that man today.

00:18:07.820 --> 00:18:10.360
Even if we ask her to cover it up,
we won't owe her anything.

00:18:10.360 --> 00:18:12.700
That's also why Mr. Hayama is here.

00:18:12.700 --> 00:18:14.360
I-Is that right?

00:18:14.360 --> 00:18:17.620
Not only that, but it made me happy.

00:18:17.620 --> 00:18:23.750
The fact that you used magic to save everyone
even if it meant possibly blowing your cover.

00:18:23.750 --> 00:18:27.290
As your older brother, I'm proud of you.

00:18:27.290 --> 00:18:28.920
Brother...

00:18:30.260 --> 00:18:31.920
Okay, we're done here!

00:18:32.340 --> 00:18:33.340
Momoka!

00:18:33.340 --> 00:18:36.550
Mommy!

00:18:36.550 --> 00:18:38.260
Big Sister!

00:18:38.260 --> 00:18:40.810
Thank you so much!

00:18:47.110 --> 00:18:48.770
Miyuki!

00:18:51.780 --> 00:18:54.200
Don't tell me that's--

00:18:54.200 --> 00:18:55.990
You don't know who might be listening.

00:18:55.990 --> 00:18:57.870
But that's...

00:18:57.870 --> 00:19:00.700
It's an inorganic object with no nerves.

00:19:00.700 --> 00:19:03.910
There's nothing wrong with rewinding it.

00:19:03.910 --> 00:19:05.540
Once again...

00:19:05.540 --> 00:19:08.420
Happy Birthday, Miyuki.

00:19:08.420 --> 00:19:10.340
Brother...

00:19:10.340 --> 00:19:11.920
Brother!

00:19:13.720 --> 00:19:18.430
Who would've thought I'd get this present
from you twice? This time around...

00:19:18.430 --> 00:19:20.930
I'm going to treasure it forever!

00:19:24.060 --> 00:19:25.690
Coconspirator?

00:19:26.190 --> 00:19:32.650
Yes. It seems like the man in question
was goaded on by an anti-magic organization.

00:19:32.650 --> 00:19:36.240
"Blanche," was it called?

00:19:36.240 --> 00:19:40.780
Master Tatsuya took care of the situation
in an extremely swift manner.

00:19:40.780 --> 00:19:45.960
Not that I don't get the feeling
that it was Miyuki who did the actual work.

00:19:47.540 --> 00:19:50.790
But since the results were satisfactory,

00:19:50.790 --> 00:19:54.510
it wouldn't do for me
to voice any objections.

00:19:54.510 --> 00:19:55.840
If you say so.

00:19:55.840 --> 00:20:01.390
I will delete as much footage
of Miyuki as possible.

00:20:01.390 --> 00:20:04.140
Don't forget to monitor the video websites.

00:20:04.140 --> 00:20:06.270
As you wish.

00:20:06.270 --> 00:20:09.560
By the way, will you be
admonishing Ms. Miyuki?

00:20:09.560 --> 00:20:12.320
That won't be necessary this time.

00:20:12.320 --> 00:20:18.030
But if this kind of thing continues,
I don't care if she is my sister's child.

00:20:18.030 --> 00:20:20.740
I will have to do something about it.

00:20:29.920 --> 00:20:32.880
So, that's this year's top freshman.

00:20:32.960 --> 00:20:37.420
FIRE INCIDENT WAS A MYSTERIOUS 
MAGICIAN INVOLVED!?

00:20:33.340 --> 00:20:35.880
I can't believe you spotted her in that.

00:20:35.880 --> 00:20:40.180
For some reason, there were
only indistinct images left.

00:20:40.180 --> 00:20:42.760
Well, who would've noticed that but me?

00:20:42.880 --> 00:20:44.140
"ENROLLED STUDENTS"

00:20:44.140 --> 00:20:47.180
"FRESHMEN"

00:20:47.180 --> 00:20:48.600
"FIRST YEAR/CLASS A"

00:20:48.600 --> 00:20:51.180
"FEATURED ARTICLE"

00:20:51.480 --> 00:20:57.110
It's so reassuring, don't you think?
Having a girl like this come to First High.

00:20:57.110 --> 00:20:59.530
You're going to have her
join the Student Council, right?

00:20:59.530 --> 00:21:03.370
Of course!
Traditionally, all top freshmen do.

00:21:03.370 --> 00:21:08.330
Too bad. I was hoping to recruit her
to join the Disciplinary Committee.

00:21:08.330 --> 00:21:12.580
But I hear that there's also a boy
around the same age.

00:21:12.580 --> 00:21:18.840
Oh? If he ends up at First High, too,
I'll drag him into my committee by force.

00:21:19.840 --> 00:21:21.390
Magic.

00:21:21.390 --> 00:21:23.470
At the dawn of the 21st century,

00:21:23.470 --> 00:21:28.770
this product of fairy tales was
systematized as an actual technology.

00:21:28.770 --> 00:21:33.060
Every nation in the world is competing
in the race to develop magicians.

00:21:33.060 --> 00:21:38.940
Here in Japan, nine magic
high schools have been established.

00:21:38.940 --> 00:21:42.700
The very fact that you've been
permitted to enroll at these schools...

00:21:42.700 --> 00:21:47.080
makes you one of the elite whose rare talent
in magic has been acknowledged.

00:21:47.080 --> 00:21:48.620
But...

00:21:51.960 --> 00:21:53.290
Miyuki...

00:21:53.290 --> 00:21:56.960
Good luck with your
class representative's speech.

00:21:56.960 --> 00:21:59.170
Thanks, Brother!

00:22:01.470 --> 00:22:05.510
...at the National Magic University
Affiliated First High School...

00:22:05.510 --> 00:22:08.430
the school we'll be attending starting today...

00:22:08.430 --> 00:22:12.020
since the moment we're enrolled,
there are "Blooms"...

00:22:12.020 --> 00:22:14.690
and "Weeds."

00:22:14.690 --> 00:22:16.440
I can't accept it!
